    {
      "id": 184017,
      "name": "MindWanderer",
      "username": "MindWanderer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-11-01T18:22:04.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Someday I will beat Kaargra without her flipping. &nbsp;Today was not that day. &nbsp;Got to 18 favor and had put both Get Back In There's on the bottom, so I thought I had it for sure. &nbsp;The only gladiator left had only 4 HP, but also Stonejaw, so I thought I was safe. &nbsp;Unfortunately, Tachyon had Chaos Lord, with Supersonic Response on the bottom, so she hit him for 2 when Sustain the Portal came out. &nbsp;I still thought I was OK (should have been 3 damage), so I was tapping through all those instances of damage pretty quickly, so I was surprised to see him die and Kaargra flip, at 19 favor (like she always does...).</p><p>Still went on to win handily, 33 to 12, Mint, with most of the party pretty healthy. &nbsp;Oblivion got Nightmist a whole mess of titles (and in retrospect, I probably would have won earlier had Thorathian Monolith not been in play, as she would have earned another title or two), and Micro-Assembler on Wraith was beautiful, letting her get out pretty much her whole collection of gear.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
