      "topic_slug": "weekly-one-shot-46-something-happened-on-the-way-to-the-beach",
      "display_username": "MindWanderer",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
      "flair_color": "",
      "flair_group_id": 41,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": "",
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Someday I will beat Kaargra without her flipping. &nbsp;Today was not that day. &nbsp;Got to 18 favor and had put both Get Back In There&#39;s on the bottom, so I thought I had it for sure. &nbsp;The only gladiator left had only 4 HP, but also Stonejaw, so I thought I was safe. &nbsp;Unfortunately, Tachyon had Chaos Lord, with Supersonic Response on the bottom, so she hit him for 2 when Sustain the Portal came out. &nbsp;I still thought I was OK (should have been 3 damage), so I was tapping through all those instances of damage pretty quickly, so I was surprised to see him die and Kaargra flip, at 19 favor (like she always does...).</p><p>Still went on to win handily, 33 to 12, Mint, with most of the party pretty healthy. &nbsp;Oblivion got Nightmist a whole mess of titles (and in retrospect, I probably would have won earlier had Thorathian Monolith not been in play, as she would have earned another title or two), and Micro-Assembler on Wraith was beautiful, letting her get out pretty much her whole collection of gear.</p>",
